 ],
 "text": "What if you got $1 every time someone said AI? Out loud, anywhere on earth, straight into your account. Day 1. A podcast plays at the gym. $14 before your second set. You buy yourself lunch and feel like a genius. Day 2. You go to one tech meetup. Two hours, four slices of free pizza, $1340. You never miss a meetup again. Week 1. Your friends work it out. Now they say it on purpose, then ask for 20%. Six of them. Same group chat. Week 3. Your bank freezes your account for suspicious activity. $61,000 and you can't even buy a coffee. Nine calls from the fraud team. Month 2. Earning season. Every CEO says it 80 times per call. You listen to 212 of them, just for fun. Month 6. $3.2 million. The tax office sets up a whole team just for you. 14 people. They have a group chat too. Year 1. Companies panic and start saying machine learning just to avoid paying you. It doesn't work. You're at $41 million. Year 3. Three governments try to ban the word. Tech conferences now sound like spy movies. $900 million. Year 10. $14 billion. More than some countries. And you still can't explain what AI actually is. What should pay you next?"
